          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "прокол (prokól) — \"a puncture\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Из-за прокола мы час стояли у дороги. Iz-za prokóla my chas stoyáli u dorógi. Because of the puncture we stood by the road for an hour."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine. У меня прокол (prokól) — I have a puncture."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "прокол (prokól) is built on проколоть 'to pierce through', from про- 'through' and колоть 'to prick, to split'. EtymDB does not list прокол (prokól); its parts are ordinary Russian."
            }
          ]
        },
